PK␀␀␀␀␀␀␀!␀~ÇMˆ␀␀ˆ␀␀X␀␀␀f020-uniform-odd-adjacent-public-20261021_v2/author/sources/accepted-c3-author/README.md# F020 odd-leading-three adjacent candidate

The bounded candidate proves original P/H squarefreeness and the original algebraic-square CD gate for n=3p^r+1, p>=5 prime, r>=2, s>r, every primitive phase. It is not independently accepted yet.

Read REPORT.md, CLAIM_SCOPE.json, SOURCE_BINDINGS.json, and CONTROL_RESULTS.json. The full accepted single-leading-digit comparison archive contains the accepted mathematical dependency and exact review. Other selected snapshots are scope comparisons only, not complete copies of those packages.

Run `python verify.py` for file/source integrity. Run `python verify.py --controls` to replay only this candidate's fresh controls and compare every JSON field; Python 3.12, NumPy and SymPy are required for the latter. No retained source program is executed. The fresh controls are bounded falsification checks, not the proof.

The central new fact is a count of L+1 nonzero strict-interior roots, not an exact zero, and the derivative separation proves them simple without a claim about individual depths. At r=2 the tied polynomial is J=XF'-F, not an unjustified globally normalized derivative residual. Its factor Y^2+1 is nonzero at the nonzero branch Y^2=-3, including p=5.

No external write, arbitrary-degree closure, FFT/cost improvement, or historical priority claim is made. A separate reviewer must bind the final frozen manifest and assess the mathematical proof.
PK␀␀␀␀␀␀␀!␀éY°O␀␀°O␀␀X␀␀␀f020-uniform-odd-adjacent-public-20261021_v2/author/sources/accepted-c3-author/REPORT.md# The first odd-leading adjacent boundary: n = 3 p^r + 1

Author candidate, 21 October 2026 UTC. Frozen local mathematical candidate for a separate independent review. No external writes. This is not self-acceptance, a historical novelty claim, arbitrary-degree closure, or an FFT/cost assertion.

## 1. The bounded theorem

Let p>=5 be prime, r>=2, s>r, N=p^r, n=3N+1, and q any characteristic-zero primitive p^s-th root. Keep exactly

    P_0=1, P_1=X, P_(j+1)=X P_j-(1-q^j)P_(j-1),
    H_j(z)=sum_a [j choose a]_q z^a,
    w_j=product_(u=1)^j (1-q^u), w_0=1.

In an algebraic p-adic embedding normalize v(q-1)=1 and set

    e=v(p)=(p-1)p^(s-1), B=r(p-1)p^(r-1)/2,
    K=3N/2+3B, E=N+3B, D=2N+3B-p=N+E-p,
    h=floor(r/2), beta=p^h, L=N/beta,
    rho=beta/2 if r is even,
    rho=p^(h-1)(2p-1)/2 if r is odd.

Then BOTH original P_n and H_n are squarefree, and the original algebraic-square Christoffel-Darboux kernel is nonzero at every P_n root.

There is no root at zero. Its exact constant valuation is

    v(P_n(0))=N+E=2N+3B.

Define x_a=i(q^(a/2)-q^(-a/2)), i^2=-1, using the square roots near 1. The beta closed disks v(X-x_a)>=rho are disjoint. Their complete root partition, counted with multiplicity before simplicity is proved, is:

* Each noncentral disk a!=0 contains 3L roots: 2L on its boundary and L in its strict interior. All these roots have v(X)=p^ord_p(a).
* The central disk contains 3L+1 roots: 2L on its boundary and L+1 in its strict interior. The interior roots are all nonzero. The theorem does not assert their individual deeper depths.

These counts total (beta-1)3L+(3L+1)=3N+1 and exhaust the degree. In particular there are no extra shallow roots at v(X)=1/2. The odd-leading residual zero has changed the central interior count from the accepted leading-digit L to L+1; it has NOT produced the exact zero present for even leading digits and odd target degree.

At every root xi, x=v(xi)>0, the ORIGINAL ordinary derivative has exact value

    v(P_n'(xi)) = min(x+D, N+E-x).                       (1.1)

The possible equality 2x=p occurs only at the central r=2 boundary and is proved noncancelling below. Centrally the formula always simplifies to

    v(P_n'(xi))=N+E-x, x>=rho.                         (1.2)

At corresponding H_n roots the ordinary derivative valuation and multiplicity are identical. These statements include every primitive phase, the p=5 boundary, and all s>r.

As a bounded corollary, the two monic discriminants have the same value

    v(Disc P_n)=v(Disc H_n)
      =3N(N+E)-[3N(p-1)/p](p-2).                      (1.3)

No claim is made for other odd leading digits, arbitrary tails or intermediate digits, p=3, r=1, s<=r, composite orders, global F020/F023 closure, speed or complexity, or historical priority.

## 2. Scope audit and exact accepted inputs

The retained accepted single-leading-digit theorem covers 1<=c<p and n=cN, including c=3. Its report explicitly gives L strict-interior roots per disk when c is odd, not only boundary roots. It also gives the coefficientwise ordinary derivative, including its constant residual at the interior root location. Its standalone accepted theorem is retained inside sources/accepted-single-leading-digit-comparison.zip; the top comparison is a bounded source comparison, not an independent second mathematical theorem review.

Exact identities of the relevant accepted theorem:

* Original author manifest: 9159078187512872a2e297b0ae0b53493d3b8ddcb39f891561d5190e2f0282cb.
* Original separate-review manifest: 3c25ca2780ab2f50537fe9c8a8442318b4d20fe6d21e58d489d8c172c2fcd636.
* Original author report: 012c2bdcf24d01c15641c938ac7b240c078ed8089e46fd9d0ebe0e34069092a6.
* Public projected report actually read: 4b603ec48cd71adb5edc22d2d5b851e8854bcd179f7913a7c0fb913529c2c120.
* Public projected separate review actually read: cfdecc094d1051d5a8863cb8ec2efeedf2a803dc71e862dcff1f6602904db0d1.

Its ACCEPTANCE.json explicitly binds both original/public report identities. The separate VERDICT.json accepts the exact cN family and the original derivative and kernel conventions. Historical source manifests bind historical bytes, not later projected public bytes; they are not silently substituted for each other. SOURCE_BINDINGS.json records current bytes, paths, archive members, scope roles and complete archive-manifest verification.

By contrast, the accepted general adjacent criterion has c even and n=cN+1. Its exact author manifest is e19104be98018ea10de85dd648b3b2634664150ea24994300e28ac56fe889ec7, accepted by separate review manifest a7990e625de81f3797ac13bbad7d7c817eb65aee195e5690f84de6ca7540c3c7. Its odd-c exclusion is explicit. The later central adjacent lift and both all-short-tail sectors likewise require even c. The retained scope controls in this packet are provenance comparisons only. The degree 3N+1 is not contained in those stated families, and c=3 is never substituted into their hypotheses.

In particular no accepted P_(3N-1) coefficientwise statement was found in the retained applicable sources. The neighboring statement in the accepted general-adjacent report is under even-c hypotheses. Section 4 below proves the specific new even neighbor and its full ordinary-derivative bound from the accepted exact Newton identities and single-leading-digit cap. It does not import neighboring squarefreeness, nor need it. The new proof uses only the accepted c=3 facts listed in Section 3 and the explicitly reproved neighbor lemma.

## 3. Applicable leading-digit input and the off-root coordinate check

Put

    A=P_(3N), M=P_(3N-1), a=1-q^(3N), F=P_(3N+1),
    Q_m=product_(j=1)^m(1-q^(2j)),
    N_m(z)=product_(j=0)^(m-1)(z+q^j),
    W(m)=sum_(j=1)^m p^ord_p(j).

All indices are below p^s: 3N+1<5N<=pN<=p^s. Thus all original edges and displayed q-factorials are nonzero, also at p=5. For positive j in the used ranges v(1-q^j)=p^ord_p(j); Q factors have 2j<=3N.

On every H disk z=-q^a+lambda Y, v(lambda)=rho, define the Gauss weights

    T(m)=sum_(j=1)^m min(p^ord_p(j),rho), R(m)=W(m)-T(m).

The accepted c=3 theorem, Sections 3-6, proves coefficientwise

    weight(N_m)>=T(m), R(m)<=W(m)/2,
    equality in the latter exactly for m=jN (0<=j<=3),
    W(N)=N+2B, W(jN)=jW(N), W((N-1)/2)=B.

W is superadditive. These are applicable c=3 assertions, not an even-c extrapolation. With omega^2=w_N and Zbar=alpha_a Y^L, alpha_a!=0,

    N_N/omega -> Zbar,
    H_(3N)/omega^3 -> M_3(Zbar)=Zbar^3+3Zbar,          (3.1)
    H_(3N)'/[C1 omega^2] -> 3 M_2(Zbar),
    M_2(Zbar)=Zbar^2+1,
    C1=w_N/[Q_A0 (1-q^(p^2))], A0=(N-p^2)/2.        (3.2)

The normalizing values are K and D respectively. The unique derivative difference pivot is k-m=p^2, but in the c=3 double sum BOTH equality pairs m=0 and m=2N occur (k=m+p^2). Their sum is the whole 3 M_2 residual, with its nonzero constant term. This differs materially from an even-leading odd derivative residual. The original derivative is taken before reduction, not obtained by differentiating M_3(alpha Y^L), which would give the wrong zero in characteristic p.

The accepted block units are

    w_(jN)/w_N^j -> j!, Q_(uN)/w_N^u -> 2^u u!,
    Q_(uN+A*)/(Q_A* w_N^u) -> 2^u u! (0<=A*<N),
    N_(jN)/omega^j -> Zbar^j.                       (3.3)

Only multipliers 0,1,2,3 below p are used. The last identity is coefficientwise and never divides by N_N at its zeros.

The exact coordinate identity, with v0 near i, is

    H_b(v0^2)=v0^b P_b(v0+v0^(-1)),
    H_b'=v0^(b-2)[(b/2)P_b+(v0-v0^(-1))P_b'/2].    (3.4)

Both coordinate derivatives are units. On the corresponding P disk, weight(A)=K, and the first term in (3.4) for b=3N has weight at least re+K>D. This strict inequality follows from re>N/2-p, since s>=r+1. Thus (3.2) transfers coefficientwise to the ordinary A' even OFF A's own roots, up to its actual nonzero analytic unit. Its residual is a scalar times M_2(Zbar). This off-root check is essential because it will be evaluated at new F roots.

For root counts, the analytic coordinate substitution preserves the disks and their residual root locations and degrees. In P coordinates take X=x_a+lambda_P Y; the leading linear coordinate factor is absorbed into alpha_a. No global P/H scalar or phase is discarded in the r=2 unit comparison below.

## 4. The new even-neighbor lemma, proved without the even-c theorem

Let b=3N-1, A*=(N-1)/2. The exact accepted Newton/ordinary-derivative identities are

    H_b=sum_(k=b mod 2) w_b N_k/[w_k Q_((b-k)/2)],     (4.1)
    H_b'=sum_(k=b mod 2,k>=1) sum_(0<=m<k)
        w_b z^(k-m-1) N_m/[Q_((b-k)/2) w_m a_(k-m)],  (4.2)
    a_j=1-q^j.

The k=0 term in (4.1) is necessary because this neighbor is EVEN. W(b)=3W(N)-N=2E. With a0=(b-k)/2, the bracket W(a0)+R(k) is at most W(b)/2=E by half-W and superadditivity. Equality requires k=lN and even parity l, hence exactly k=0,2N. At these two values equality is attained: a0=N+A* or A*, respectively. Set the actual scalar

    Cminus=omega^4/[a_(3N) Q_A*], v(Cminus)=E.

Using (3.3), the k=0 term divided by Cminus has residue 3, and the k=2N term has residue 3 Zbar^2. Every other term has strictly higher weight. Therefore

    H_(3N-1)/Cminus -> 3 M_2(Zbar).                 (4.3)

For the WHOLE ordinary derivative (4.2), write j=k-m>=1. The term's subtracted valuation bracket is bounded by

    W(a0)+R(m)+p^ord_p(j)
      <= W(b-j)/2+p^ord_p(j)
       = E+[p^ord_p(j)-W(j)/2].                    (4.4)

Reflection here is exact: ord_p(3N-u)=ord_p(u) for 1<=u<3N. If u is a nonzero multiple of N, its multiplier and its complement in 3 are 1 or 2, both units since p>=5. This gives W(b-j)=W(b)-W(j).

At fixed d=ord_p(j), the final square bracket is maximized at j=p^d and equals [p^d-d(p-1)p^(d-1)]/2. It is 1/2 only at j=1 or p, negative for d>=2, and strictly decreases at larger j of fixed order. For j=1 or p, parity of k makes m ODD. If m is not a multiple of N the half-W bound is strict. If m is a multiple of N, the only permitted odd multiplier is m=N. Then 2a0=2N-1-j, with floor(2a0/N)=1 and floor(a0/N)=0, so 2W(a0)<W(2a0) already at the N-level floor term. Thus in every case the bracket in (4.4) is strictly below E+1/2. All brackets belong to (1/2)Z, so they are at most E. Every derivative term has weight at least E.

The exact coordinate identity (3.4), now b=3N-1, transfers these full bounds to

    weight(M)>=E, weight(M')>=E,                   (4.5)

and (4.3) to M up to its actual unit. There is no simplicity inference from this lemma. It establishes exactly the coefficientwise facts required later, including the formerly absent constant neighbor residual.

## 5. Full even transfer and the changed zero location

Parity from the original recurrence makes A odd, M even and F even. The exact transfer is

    F=X A-a M, v(a)=N.                             (5.1)

This is F itself, not F/X. Division by X would not give a polynomial because F(0)=-a M(0)!=0. Centrally (4.3) at Y=0 has constant 3, a unit, so v(M(0))=E and v(F(0))=N+E. This also agrees with the exact even constant product F(0)=(-1)^((3N+1)/2) product_(j odd,1<=j<=3N)(1-q^j).

On a noncentral disk X has constant valuation x_a0=p^ord_p(a)<rho. Thus XA has Gauss weight K+x_a0 and its reduction is a nonzero scalar times M_3(Zbar). The correction has weight at least N+E=K+N/2, strictly greater since x_a0<rho<N/2. The scaled F reduction has degree 3L, with residual zero of multiplicity L and two nonzero residual locations each of multiplicity L.

On the central disk the weight of XA is K+rho, also strictly below N+E. Here the reduction is a nonzero scalar times

    Y M_3(alpha_0 Y^L)
       =alpha_0 Y^(L+1)(alpha_0^2 Y^(2L)+3).        (5.2)

It has degree 3L+1, zero multiplicity L+1, and two nonzero residual locations each of multiplicity L. Since p>=5, the Hermite nonzero roots are distinct and nonzero.

Each normalized translated polynomial is integral, the stated degree has unit leading coefficient, and all coefficients above that degree have positive valuation. Closed-disk Newton/Weierstrass counting therefore gives precisely the counts of Section 1, including residual multiplicity counts in the strict interiors. This is not simple-root Hensel lifting of the inseparable Y^L substitution. The counts sum to the degree, hence give a complete all-root cover without a separate assumption about interior depths. At every F root, including central and noncentral interior roots, M_3(Zbar)=0. Because M_2 is 1 at Zbar=0 and -2 at Zbar^2=-3, (3.2)-(4.3) yield

    v(M(xi))=E, v(A'(xi))=D.                      (5.3)

The entire point of the odd-leading proof is that (5.3) stays valid on the residual ZERO branch. No missing higher lifting lemma is needed merely to prove simplicity there.

## 6. Ordinary derivative separation, including the central interior

Every F root is nonzero by Section 5. At a root xi with x=v(xi), (5.1) gives A(xi)=a M(xi)/xi. Ordinary differentiation BEFORE reduction gives

    F'(xi)=a M(xi)/xi+xi A'(xi)-a M'(xi).           (6.1)

The exact values of the first two summands and the bound on the third are

    N+E-x, x+D, at least N+E.                      (6.2)

The third is strictly higher than the first since x>0. The difference between the first two values is p-2x. Whenever 2x!=p, the uniquely smaller term proves (1.1) and nonvanishing.

All noncentral x are integral powers of an odd prime, hence cannot equal p/2. In the central disk rho=p/2 exactly when r=2 and rho>p/2 when r>=3. Every strict-interior root has x>rho>=p/2, so its derivative is governed by the FIRST term and has value N+E-x. In particular no attempt is made to treat those L+1 roots as boundary roots or infer their individual x. The same separation covers the entire central disk for r>=3. The sole remaining case is the 2p central boundary roots at r=2.

An equivalent polynomial identity, useful for the tied case, is

    J:=X F'-F=X^2 A'+a M-a X M'.                   (6.3)

At a root J=XF'. Using J avoids an erroneous off-root claim about the much lower leading residual of F' itself.

## 7. The r=2 central tie: actual units and no obstruction

Let N=p^2, B=N-p, rho=p/2, L=p, t=q-1, and choose mu^2=t^p, X=mu Y. Use the branch v0 near i. The exact edge initial is

    (1-q^j)/t^(p^ord_p(j)) -> -j/p^ord_p(j).

The elementary full-block products give

    w_N/t^(N+2B) -> -1,
    Q_A*/t^B -> -1, A*=(N-1)/2,
    a_(3N)/t^N -> -3,
    N_N(z)/(t^B mu^p) -> -i^p Y^p.                (7.1)

For the first product, multiply the nonmultiples-of-p blocks and the p-divisible block. For Q_A*, write A*=ap+a, a=(p-1)/2; the product of reduced indices is (-1)^a(a!)^2=-1 by Wilson, and (-2)^A*=1. For N_N, the p indices divisible by p contribute (z+1)^p to the initial and the others contribute -t^B; use the exact z+1=v0 X. These are unit calculations, not sign fitting from a control.

Write eta for the residue of omega/(t^B mu^p), so eta^2=-1, and delta=-i^p/eta. Then delta^2=1 and Zbar=delta Y^p. The central nonzero residual roots of F therefore satisfy

    Y^(2p)=-3, equivalently Y^2=-3.                (7.2)

The equivalence uses Frobenius in the algebraically closed residue field; both -3 and delta^2 are in the prime field. Odd parity does not allow the even-c global normalizing scalar to be copied, but (7.2) does not require that scalar.

Now compare the ACTUAL scalar normalizations in (3.2) and (4.3). Their common residual factor is 3M_2(Zbar), nonzero at every root under discussion. Before any division at a root, their normalizing-scalar ratio is exactly

    (C1 omega^2)/Cminus
        =a_(3N) Q_A*/[Q_A0 a_(p^2)].               (7.3)

For r=2, A0=0; its initial is -3 t^B by (7.1). In transferring the H derivative-to-neighbor ratio to P, the exact unit multiplier from (3.4) is 2v0^2/(v0^2-1), whose residue is 1. The omitted A prefactor has already been proved strictly higher. Consequently, coefficientwise on this disk,

    A'/(t^B S_M) -> -3 mbar(Y),
    M/S_M -> mbar(Y),                              (7.4)

where S_M is any actual scalar of value E normalizing M and mbar is its actual residue, a nonzero constant times M_2(delta Y^p)=Y^(2p)+1. We do not need to choose its otherwise phase-dependent constant.

In J from (6.3), the first two terms have weight N+E because p+D=N+E. The last has weight at least N+E+rho, strictly higher. Since mu^2=t^p and B+p=N, (7.1),(7.4) give the POLYNOMIAL coefficientwise residual

    J(mu Y)/(t^N S_M)
         -> -3 (Y^2+1) mbar(Y).                   (7.5)

At every root from (7.2), both Y^2+1 and Y^(2p)+1 equal -2, which is nonzero for p>=5. Thus J has exact value N+E there, so F'=J/X has exact value N+E-rho=D+rho. This proves the tie case in (1.1), including p=5 without a deeper correction. The obstruction that appears for even leading digits is absent on this particular odd-leading nonzero branch.

It would be WRONG to write (7.5) as the coefficientwise residual of F' normalized to D+rho: F' includes A and generally has a lower off-root weight. Formula (7.5) is for J, and its use for F' is explicitly at F roots. No ordinary-derivative integer factor or H coordinate unit is suppressed.

## 8. H squarefreeness, all phases, and the algebraic-square kernel

Modulo the maximal ideal P_n=X^n and H_n=(1+z)^n. P roots therefore are not +/-2; H_n has nonzero constant coefficient. In (3.4), both ordinary coordinate derivatives are units. At a corresponding root the P_n prefactor term vanishes EXACTLY, transferring multiplicities and derivative values from P_n to H_n. Every derivative value proved above is finite, so both polynomials are squarefree.

Every recurrence edge a_j for 1<=j<n is nonzero. If P_n and P_(n-1) had a common root, backward recurrence would force P_0=1 to vanish. The ORIGINAL ordinary Christoffel-Darboux identity at a P_n root xi is

    sum_(j=0)^(n-1) P_j(xi)^2/w_j
       =P_n'(xi) P_(n-1)(xi)/w_(n-1).              (8.1)

All right-hand factors are nonzero. The summands are algebraic squares, not absolute-value squares. No positivity, interlacing, real-root or Fourier argument is used. Injectivity of the algebraic p-adic embedding and Galois conjugacy transfer these nonvanishing statements to every characteristic-zero primitive phase.

For (1.3), exactly m=3L(beta-beta/p)=3N(p-1)/p roots have x=1: they are precisely the noncentral disks with a a p-unit. All others have x>=p/2, and their derivative values are N+E-x, including the tie. The product of all roots has value N+E from F(0), so their x values sum to N+E. Summing (1.1) gives

    m(D+1)+(n-m)(N+E)-[(N+E)-m]
      =3N(N+E)-m(p-2).

This uses no unproved individual interior depth. The monic H discriminant has the same derivative-value sum by the established unit correspondence.

## 9. Controls, provenance, and review gate

check_controls.py is a fresh bounded transcription/falsification check, not a proof by sampling and not an imported accepted program. It checks:

* Original symbolic recurrence identities J=XF'-F and the exact even constant product at target degrees 4,6,8; the M3/M2 resultant is 4 and the tied factor remainder modulo Y^2+3 is -2.
* The complete new neighbor equality set k=0,2N and every ordinary derivative summand bracket in three small parameter choices (5,2),(5,3),(7,2), not a rank or degree census.
* Two actual original-recurrence cyclotomic controls: (p,r,s)=(5,2,3), (5,3,4). Arithmetic is in (Z/125)[q]/Phi_(p^s)(q), with complete q-basis and complete X polynomial, followed by exact q=1+t Pascal substitution. Coefficient values are j+e ord_p(c_j), j<e, and their initial units include p/t^e=-1. Distinct j<e have distinct weights modulo e. Precision 3e is strictly above all tested thresholds; no characteristic-p shortcut discards mixed-characteristic derivative factors.

The r=2 control includes the actual J residual (not a formally differentiated inseparable residual). The r=3 comparison retains alpha_a-dependent units, comparing phase-covariant Hermite coefficient relations instead of imposing r=2 signs at r=3. All checks pass. There is no numerical root solver, finite-field squarefreeness proxy, rank census, or execution of supplied source modules.

The uniform proof is Sections 3-8. The sources, proof, scope, control code and results are frozen by MANIFEST.json and SEAL.json. A separate independent reviewer must bind those exact bytes before acceptance. No publication or external repository write is part of this candidate.
