This is the separate mathematical review of the exact frozen uniform odd-leading adjacent candidate identified in VERDICT.json and SOURCE_BINDING.json. It accepts only the explicitly bounded family stated there, using the original P, H, ordinary derivatives, and algebraic-square kernel. It does not claim global F020/F023 closure or historical novelty.

Read INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md for the full reasoning, including the genuine first-layer obstruction and its odd-operator second-layer resolution. The source snapshots are evidence copies, not complete source packages; their external manifest identities are retained distinctly.

Run `python verify.py --expect-manifest HASH` with the independently supplied review manifest hash to check every byte. Add `--replay` to rerun only the three newly authored reviewer programs in a disposable directory and compare their result files byte-for-byte. Neither path executes any producer or dependency program. Replay needs Python 3, NumPy, and SymPy. It uses exact arithmetic, not floating point.

The scripts in private/ are the research controls and their outputs. Finite controls are falsification diagnostics; the unlimited-family proof is in the reviewed report and independent review. No source or external repository is modified by this package.
